{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0281","math_ordinal":286,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Without parentheses the epsilon term lies outside the n-sum and leaves n free; the next bound uses the sum of both n-indexed terms over the disjoint partition.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt265.tex:359","source_normalized_sha256":"12d6e3fecebcb342f6a38157f5c0b2a33bc5051ae53591134fc6ca478be4f5d7","source_text":"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}J_n\\mu_r^*D_n+\\epsilon\\mu_r^*D_n$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt265.tex:355","target_normalized_sha256":"444f9623782713af7d551b2fbb1f08a8921c6958ed4ea4645b95b70ed301edab","target_text":"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(J_n\\mu_r^*D_n+\\epsilon\\mu_r^*D_n)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S265"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-measure-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0282","math_ordinal":286,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The section defines mu_r as Lebesgue measure and uses it throughout; no unindexed measure mu is bound in this theorem.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt265.tex:363","source_normalized_sha256":"12d6e3fecebcb342f6a38157f5c0b2a33bc5051ae53591134fc6ca478be4f5d7","source_text":"$\\int_D\\sum_nJ_n\\chi D_n\\,d\\mu$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt265.tex:358","target_normalized_sha256":"444f9623782713af7d551b2fbb1f08a8921c6958ed4ea4645b95b70ed301edab","target_text":"$\\int_D\\sum_nJ_n\\chi D_n\\,d\\mu_r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S265"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-measure-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0283","math_ordinal":293,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The theorem's integration measure is mu_r and no unindexed mu is defined; the following terms and conclusion all use mu_r.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt265.tex:371","source_normalized_sha256":"453eb713db4ba032a9e7976bc409ba39f401c12bcaffc47f4e3e28aa84de0782","source_text":"$\\int_DJ\\,d\\mu$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt265.tex:367","target_normalized_sha256":"1e5b58421132b004a039b560d2e258b3e3bbb8c488eb0ac5899e447e7e0dbfa1","target_text":"$\\int_DJ\\,d\\mu_r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S265"}
